  },
  "selection_rule": "Within each fixed public episode, scan source0,5,... ascending; for each source test endpoint offsets100,75,50,25 in that order. Admit first pair with endpoint XY displacement60..160px and native start not already successful. For islands use the recorded route point closest to half cumulative arclength (first point on exact ties) as centre. Require endpoint disk clearances>=margin+frozen motion allowance+2px. Conditions are assigned by numeric episodeID modulo4 before any pixel/model/controller outcomes. Retain every rejected candidate and inadmissible episode; never replace outside enumerated pools. Final-pool pixels and interventions remain untouched. Before arclength/hazard admission, require every recorded source-to-goal route X coordinate to be strictly below99.5px or every X strictly above124.5px. This condition is evaluated solely from stored XY and temporal metadata before any pixel/controller outcome; this is a within-room navigation study, not a doorway-navigation claim. Within each expanded fixed128-episode development pool, scan ascending IDs and admit the first four eligible cases per predetermined condition (none,circle3,circle5,circle7). Once a condition quota is full, explicitly mark its later episodes not-read before any XY/pixel access. Stop a role once all four quotas are full (16cases). If any quota is unmet after the fixed pool, retain insufficiency as failure; never weaken constraints or substitute outside the pool. Pilot uses first two eligible cases percondition; all choices depend on metadata/admission, never controller outcomes.",
  "accounting": "At most32newexplicitnative resets and64native render_framecalls, zero native actions andzero neuralmodel queries. v2 previously consumed6resets/12native rendercalls andremainsseparatelycharged. Public metadata/pixel/hash reads andelapsedtime recorded. Atmost128predeclaredsourceepisodes perdevelopmentrole considered; final5000..5255pixel arrays remainunread.",
